WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.000
Plenty of questions are left to be answered
in Episode IX, and Star Wars fans can only

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.720
hold out hope that it will deliver.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:12.380
From Rey's true heritage to Lando Calrissian's
return, these are just some of the biggest

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.820
questions fans have going into The Rise of
Skywalker.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.480
One of the biggest mysteries within this new
trilogy has centered on Rey, an extremely

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.360
talented Jedi in training who, one might assume,
comes from talented stock.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.640
Much like Luke Skywalker, who ended up serving
as her mentor in The Last Jedi, Rey clearly

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.000
comes from a storied family, and in The Force
Awakens, it seemed like the next one or two

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.160
installments might clear up who her parents
truly were and whether or not she was a Skywalker,

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.300
a Solo, or a member of another powerful legacy
clan.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:46.769
In The Last Jedi, Kylo Ren broke the news
to Rey that she was nothing but the child

00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:52.109
of, quote, "junk traders" but naturally, most
fans don't believe that a Jedi with such natural

00:00:52.109 --> 00:00:57.140
talent who seems poised to take up the lightsaber
of someone like Luke Skywalker came from a

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.420
clan of nobodies.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.040
Will The Rise of Skywalker reveal that she's
actually a Skywalker?

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.920
All we can do is wait and find out.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:09.260
Introduced in The Force Awakens, Maz Kanata
has left audiences curious since her first

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.300
moment onscreen.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.740
A wise being who is apparently over a thousand
years old, Maz is as inscrutable as she is

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.980
sarcastic and endlessly endearing.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:23.020
When we meet Maz, she's managing a bar on
the planet of Takodana where she seems to

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.400
know every person and everything about them.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:31.289
She also just happens to be in possession
of a pretty damn important object: Luke Skywalker's

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:33.700
lightsaber, which she says "calls to" Rey.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:42.300
"That lightsaber was Luke's and his father's
before him and now, it calls to you."

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.060
Maz Kanata is capable of using the Force,
so there are plenty of reasons why she might

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:52.100
have Luke's lightsaber one of the most important
items in the entire Star Wars saga but it's

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.810
still unexplained when, if, or how exactly
Maz met Luke.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.220
Who is Maz, and where did she come from?

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.520
How did she know Luke?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.679
How did she get his lightsaber, and how did
she use the Force to ascertain that it should

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.440
go to Rey?

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:10.500
In an Episode IX teaser released in April
of 2019, audiences clearly heard the distinctive

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.940
chuckle of Emperor Palpatine, one of the signature
villains of the original trilogy and the prequels.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:20.860
As the Sith master of the infamous Darth Vader,
the Emperor is an imposing figure throughout

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:25.470
the series, bringing the Sith back from the
brink of extinction while serving as the Emperor

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.200
of the entire Galactic Empire.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.480
The Emperor is also known for exterminating
various Jedi that he sees as potential threats.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.220
He's also ALSO known for, well being dead.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:42.900
Ahh, that's never not satisfying Anywho, even
though Darth Vader ultimately redeems himself

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:48.050
by killing the Emperor in The Return of the
Jedi, Palpatine's evil laugh is clearly featured

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.560
at the end of the first Rise of Skywalker
teaser.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:55.700
Surprisingly, director J.J. Abrams has already
confirmed that the Emperor will appear in

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.200
the film still played by actor Ian McDiarmid.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:02:59.900
"I, uhh…

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.800
I have to be honest with you.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:07.280
I was in the area, so I thought the least
I could do is to pop in for a laugh."

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.931
McDiarmid has said the character is definitely
dead heading into The Rise of Skywalker, but

00:03:11.931 --> 00:03:16.400
what role will he play in the final installment
of the series and what form will he be taking

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.580
when he does return?

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.000
Fans of the original trilogy fell in love
with Billy Dee Williams' portrayal of the

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.920
roguish if wishy-washy Lando Calrissian.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:30.080
Audiences last got to see a younger Lando
played by the devilishly charming Donald Glover

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.600
in Solo: A Star Wars Story, which told the
origin story of his relationship with Han.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.160
"Is this seat taken?"

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.420
"If nobody's in the seat, then it ain't taken,
friend."

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.860
But in The Rise of Skywalker, the original
Lando will return.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:50.350
Williams is reprising his role in Episode
IX, closing one of the longest gaps between

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:53.300
portrayals of the same character in cinematic
history.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.260
Even though it's exciting to hear that one
of the original trilogy's most popular and

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:02.520
beloved characters will finally return, it
also remains a mystery exactly why Lando is

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:07.660
back, especially considering that he was conspicuously
absent from this trilogy's first two films.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.880
What role will he play in the story?

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.440
How will he react to the news that Han died
at the hands of his own son?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:17.760
Finally, will he side with the Resistance,
or turn sides when it becomes convenient for

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.260
him?

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:24.020
The sudden death of Carrie Fisher in 2016
was incredibly devastating to Star Wars fans.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:30.259
"Carrie Fisher, whose role as Princess Leia
in Star Wars vaulted her to pop culture immortality,

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.840
died today in Los Angeles."

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.280
After all, her portrayal of an older Leia
Organa who'd become a Resistance general without

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:40.340
losing any of her grit was an unexpected turn
between trilogies.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.659
Considering that many believed Episode IX
would feature Leia in an even bigger role

00:04:44.659 --> 00:04:49.319
than the relatively significant ones she played
in VII and VIII, it remains to be seen how

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.260
she will actually appear on screen.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:56.040
J.J. Abrams and others have revealed that,
thanks to unused footage from the first two

00:04:56.050 --> 00:05:01.090
films, it's possible for Fisher to posthumously
appear in The Rise of Skywalker without resorting

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:05.830
to a CGI version of her character though fans
might prefer that her last appearance end

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.260
on an ambiguous note.

00:05:07.669 --> 00:05:12.639
Still, considering that Han died in The Force
Awakens and Luke died in The Last Jedi, there's

00:05:12.639 --> 00:05:16.830
a decent chance that this final film will
see Leia joining her departed friends and

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:17.820
loved ones.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.699
It's clear that the storied Skywalker name
is still of the utmost importance in the sequel

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:27.900
trilogy reinforced by the news that Episode
IX's official title is The Rise of Skywalker.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.280
Of course, this led to plenty of questions
about what that means and how it reflects

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.200
on the plot of this final installment.

00:05:34.669 --> 00:05:39.760
Kylo Ren may have told Rey that she came from,
quote, "nobody," but director J.J. Abrams

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.330
seems determined to return to the mystery
he set up in The Force Awakens, telling fans

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:48.440
that the identity of Rey's parents will still
prove important in Episode IX.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:53.320
It's possible that Rey, who possesses a stunning
amount of power for such a young, untrained

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.260
Jedi, could still be the titular Skywalker.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:01.160
Aside from her, Kylo Ren is technically half
Skywalker on his mother's side, and could

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.009
turn back to the light and reclaim his heritage.

00:06:04.009 --> 00:06:08.039
It's even possible that a new character could
take up the Skywalker mantle and rise to fight

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.300
alongside our heroes.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.650
With all that said, the biggest question still
stands who is the Skywalker in the title,

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:17.060
and what purpose will they serve in Episode
IX?

